# Reverting a previously staged modification to HEAD and adding again
# must cancel staging, rather than create an unchanged commit.
I definitions.inc
> init
<<<
+ wug.txt wug.txt
> add wug.txt
<<<
> commit "base"
<<<
+ wug.txt notwug.txt
> add wug.txt
<<<
E .gitlet/Stage/Addition/wug.txt
+ wug.txt wug.txt
> add wug.txt
<<<
* .gitlet/Stage/Addition/wug.txt
> commit "should not exist"
No changes added to the commit.
<<<
# Also cancel a removal when the original content is restored.
> rm wug.txt
<<<
E .gitlet/Stage/Remove/wug.txt
+ wug.txt wug.txt
> add wug.txt
<<<
* .gitlet/Stage/Remove/wug.txt
* .gitlet/Stage/Addition/wug.txt
> commit "also should not exist"
No changes added to the commit.
<<<
> log
===
${COMMIT_HEAD}
base

===
${COMMIT_HEAD}
initial commit

<<<*
